-- title:
--   Components of the special fibre of X₁(Mp): I₁ I₂ = Iₛ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $L \subset \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), assumed nonzero. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra of characteristic $p$, and write $X_k = \mathrm{pullback}$ of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $i_1, i_2$ be closed immersions of $C_1$, $C_2$ into $X_k$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, whose images together cover the points of $X_k$, with $\mathrm{pullback}\, i_1\, i_2$ reduced of cardinality $n > 0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O : A \to O$ carrying the maximal ideal of $A$ onto that of $O$, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O =$ the structure map $A \to k$; let $bc : X_k \to X_O$ be a morphism of the two pullbacks commuting with the projection to the model and inducing $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ on bases. Then the kernel ideal sheaves of $i_1$ followed by $bc$ and of $i_2$ followed by $bc$ are invertible, in the sense that every point of $X_O$ has an affine open $U$ and $f \in \Gamma(X_O, U)$ with the point in the basic open of $f$ such that the ideal on the affine basic open of $f$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor, and the product of these two ideal sheaves equals the kernel ideal sheaf of $bc$.
--
--   This is the statement that, after the unramified base change $A \to O$, the special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ is the sum of its two components as a divisor: the two component ideal sheaves are Cartier and their product is the ideal sheaf of the whole fibre. It feeds the subsequent construction of the relative effective Cartier divisor pair, of the associated rigidified line bundle, and of the Euler-characteristic computation on this model.
-- source:
